    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n`membershipNumber` is a value **derived** from an owner's own persisted fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), not something to store or compute in the request pipeline. That makes it exactly like the existing read-only derived fields `displayName` and `initials`, so I put it in the same place:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` and a small `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method that formats `<customerCode>-M<YY>` via `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)`. It returns `null` when either source field is absent, mirroring the surrounding style while avoiding an NPE for owners lacking those fields.\n\nNo new pipeline steps or entity columns were needed \u2014 the logic lives in the single place that already owns Owner\u2192DTO derivation, keeping each class focused.\n\nResult: `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
